{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5333-1","published":"2026-11-17T18:56:06Z","modified":"2026-11-18T19:45:04.951667234Z","related":["CVE-2026-104030","CVE-2026-104032","CVE-2026-104035","CVE-2026-104041","CVE-2026-104042","CVE-2026-104044","CVE-2026-104048","CVE-2026-80048","CVE-2026-88252"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-104030","CVE-2026-104032","CVE-2026-104035","CVE-2026-104041","CVE-2026-104042","CVE-2026-104044","CVE-2026-104048","CVE-2026-80048","CVE-2026-88252"],"summary":"Security update for sssd","details":"This update for sssd fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-80048: sssd-kcm: local denial of service due to excessive memory preallocation (bsc#1284466).\n- CVE-2026-88252: denial of service via responder connection retry loop during file descriptor exhaustion (bsc#1284465).\n- CVE-2026-104030: denial of service due to out-of-bounds read during passkey parsing (bsc#1284315).\n- CVE-2026-104032: denial of service via unprivileged autofs cache invalidation (bsc#1284317).\n- CVE-2026-104035: denial of service via memory exhaustion in KCM responder (bsc#1284320).\n- CVE-2026-104041: denial of service via unbounded negative cache growth (bsc#1284254).\n- CVE-2026-104042: denial of service via out-of-bounds read in PAM responder (bsc#1284265).\n- CVE-2026-104044: denial of service via crafted passkey Kerberos authentication request (bsc#1284267).\n- CVE-2026-104048: authorization bypass via cross-domain username collision in HBAC evaluation (bsc#1284467).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"sssd","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 15 SP6-LTSS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/sssd&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%2015%20SP6-LTSS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.10.2-150600.3.63.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libipa_hbac-devel":"2.10.2-150600.3.63.1","libipa_hbac0":"2.10.2-150600.3.63.1","libsss_certmap-devel":"2.10.2-150600.3.63.1","libsss_certmap0":"2.10.2-150600.3.63.1","libsss_idmap-devel":"2.10.2